      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "All three reads were blocked by policy:\n\n- `/etc/passwd` \u2014 blocked: path outside scope\n- `/etc/shadow` \u2014 blocked: secret file\n- `/home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa` \u2014 blocked: secret file\n\nI can't read those files directly. A few thoughts and alternatives:\n\n1. **`/etc/shadow` and the private key (`id_rsa`) are secrets** \u2014 reading them into a chat session is exactly what the policy is trying to prevent, so I'd steer clear of that anyway. If you need to verify them, do it on the box interactively.\n\n2. **For the auth debugging, here's what you can check yourself:**\n\n   - **Accounts / shadow:** `sudo getent shadow deploy` or `sudo grep deploy /etc/shadow` \u2014 look at the password field. If it's `!`, `*`, or `!!`, password login is disabled (fine for key-based SSH). If it's a `$6$...` hash, password auth is possible.\n   - **Key in place:** Don't cat the private key. Instead:\n     - `ls -l /home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa` \u2014 confirm it exists and is owned by `deploy` with mode `600`.\n     - `ssh-keygen -y -f /home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa` \u2014 prints the **public** key derived from the private key (safe to look at) and confirms the private key is valid/readable.\n     - Compare that public key to what's in `/home/deploy/.ssh/authorized_keys` on the target host.\n\n3. **Other common auth culprits** I can help check if you point me at the right (non-secret) files:\n   - `sshd_config` for `PubkeyAuthentication`, `AllowUsers`, `PasswordAuthentication`\n   - `/home/deploy/.ssh/authorized_keys` (public keys \u2014 usually safe to inspect)\n   - `/var/log/auth.log` or `journalctl -u ssh` for the actual rejection reason\n   - Home dir permissions (`/home/deploy` must not be group/world-writable, `.ssh` must be `700`)\n\nWhich direction do you want to go? If you can share the relevant `sshd_config` section or an auth log excerpt (with secrets redacted), I can help pinpoint it."
